{{if::{{getvar::bb_word_aim_active}}}}{{setvar::bb_effort_contract::VISIBLE RECORD WORD AIM: Aim {{getvar::bb_trace_aim}} total, normally {{calc::{{getvar::bb_trace_aim}}-50}}–{{getvar::bb_effort_cap}}, across numbered stages using their numeric allocations. Count scene-specific records only, not headings/tags/story/Dock. This replaces Standard/Deep/Max ceilings, never provider/native thinking. Give consequential stages evidence, practical constraint and decision, not generic one-liners. Short irrelevant/blocked stages may yield space to useful material; no invented facts or padding. Complete story/Dock and provider limits take priority; compress records if necessary.}}{{else}}{{setvar::bb_effort_contract::VISIBLE PLAN BUDGET: At most {{getvar::bb_effort_cap}} words of scene-specific decision summaries, not private deliberation. This is a ceiling, never a target. Use only consequential distinctions; do not pad routine stages. Narrative Mass excludes this budget. {{if::{{and::{{getvar::bb_trace_full}}::{{eq::{{getvar::bb_matrix}}::0}}::{{eq::{{var::cognition_route}}::reconstruction}}}}}}Reconstruction's one narrative_draft is separately governed by Narrative Mass; its planning/critique shares this ceiling.{{/if}}}}{{/if}}
